## About this project

Software Factory 26 is an installable software factory: fourteen Agent Skills
that take an idea or a GitHub issue to shipped, verified, documented code,
with an orchestrator that delegates the work to sub-agents instead of doing
it inline.

It is inspired by the JSM engineering workflow and by Leon van Zyl's
production skills, and it credits both.

## Contributing

Open an issue or a pull request. If you are changing how the factory
orchestrates, read `ARCHITECTURE.md` first: the two planes, the three seams
and the one vocabulary are the load-bearing parts, and a change that breaks
the seam will look fine locally and fail in a worker.

Run `npm run check` before you push. It is dependency-free and takes under a
second.

